@title STORY • DESTINY: SAY WHAT YOU WANT
@bg chicago_street_day
You're Destiny. Junior. Hurdles. Chicago, the summer before college. Your mom's beauty supply store. You've been working the register since you were twelve.
Your mom: If you want something, baby, you say it. Clear. People can't read minds. And the ones who say they can are lying.
@bg track_stadium_day
@show coachlewis
Coach Lewis: Destiny. Your trail leg is three degrees off. I can see it from the press box.
Destiny: Coach. Nobody can see three degrees from the press box.
Coach Lewis: I can.
He's right. He's always right. It's infuriating.
> [Good] "Show me. Slow motion. I'll fix it today." -> a1
> [Bitchy] "Then come down from the press box and show me, Coach." -> a2
*a1
@add Discipline 3
Coach Lewis: (almost smiling) This is why you're my favorite. Don't tell Cassie.
Destiny: Cassie thinks she's your favorite.
Coach Lewis: Cassie thinks a lot of things.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Discipline 2
He comes down. He shows you. In his dress shoes. He clears the hurdle perfectly. The whole team stops to stare. You will respect him forever.
*a_done
@bg locker_room
@show cassie
Cassie is sitting on the bench. She just got out-leaned at the line and missed a PR by a hundredth.
Cassie: Destiny. How do you never cry?
> [Sweet] "I cry. In my car. Every week. Nobody knows." -> b1
> [Good] "I cry when it matters. This one doesn't. Next week does." -> b2
> [Bold] "I don't cry. I get mad and then I get faster." -> b3
*b1
@add Cassie_Bond 3
Cassie: (eyes huge) You're telling ME? The biggest gossip on this TEAM?
Destiny: Yeah. 'Cause I know you won't tell.
Cassie never tells. Not that one. Not ever.
@jump end
*b2
@add Cassie_Bond 2
Cassie: (sniffling) That's so mature. I hate it.
@jump end
*b3
@add Cassie_Bond 1
Cassie: (standing up, determined) Okay. I'm mad. I'm mad! I'm getting faster!
She does a lap. She is not faster. But she's smiling.
*end
Destiny has spent two years telling everybody on the team to just say what they want. This year, a few of them listened.
